-- statement:
--   The theorem states that the defined proposition MainTarget holds, a planar Falconer-type distance set statement. Here the plane is two-dimensional Euclidean space ℝ², and the distance set of a set E is the set of all real numbers r equal to the distance between some pair of points x and y of E. MainTarget says that for every compact subset E of the plane whose Hausdorff dimension is strictly greater than 1, the distance set of E has strictly positive Lebesgue measure (volume) in ℝ. In the source this theorem is admitted without proof.
